this morning on the dish as you may be  preparing for your socially distanced  labor day barbecue  we're taking you to a place few people  ever get to see  inside a president's kitchen chef  matthew wendell went from his small town  in texas to cooking for world leaders as  an aide to president george w  bush his story and his recipes are now  available in his new cookbook  recipes from the president's ranch chris  van cleeve met up with him  at wendell's outdoor kitchen are you  sure i can handle this  anyone can make burgers this way we'll  see about that  while the burger is a labor day staple  it's one i've  never made from scratch when i walk down  here the first thing i do is look around  and look for the microwave  i notice we're not using the microwave i  don't even own a microwave  you don't own a microwave no old fashion  so a cook i am not fortunately mr old  fashioned here matthew wendell  very much is he never set out to be a  chef  but has been working in the kitchen  since he was a kid a love of food born  from helping his mother velva  cook for his eight siblings as soon as  we were  old enough to sit on the counter and  stir something she thought that if you  could cook you would never go hungry and  you could always find a job  it would be years and a couple of career  changes later while working as a caterer  in austin when he befriended then texas  governor george w  bush and his wife laura about a year  before  bush announced he was running for  president he asked wendell who he calls  maddie  if he'd come with him to washington were  there points when you were  there that you're like how did i end up  here i always told mrs bush  it's surreal i mean i'm just a cook  learned in my mother's kitchen and  you're having me cook for all these very  important people  and she said that's the way we want it  like the book says  food people like to eat in maddie's new  cookbook recipes from the president's  ranch  food people like to eat this soft-spoken  small-town texan  takes us on his unlikely but very tasty  journey from washing dishes in the back  of phillips and danbury texas  to the oval office and the kitchens at  camp david  and president bush's crawford texas  ranch revealing these pictures few have  seen before  what was president bush's favorite meal  i would say dessert  crawford was the bush family's retreat  from washington when they were at the  ranch  wendell was in the kitchen making meals  like the one he made for us  from recipes he's now sharing with  everyone at the urging  of the former first lady today we're  having the smokey cheeseburgers  pasta salad fried chicken of course some  salsa and chips that made the salsa  a lower bushes peach cream pie and my  chocolate chip cookies  and the chocolate chip cookies these  were a staple  a staple president's ranch every time we  went to the ranch or camp david  we had to have cookies the ranch became  a key part of presidential diplomacy  hosting world leaders like russian  president vladimir putin  british prime minister tony blair and  mexican president vincente fox  often it was wendell's food that brought  them together  you're making some of these meals for a  world leader do you feel some extra  pressure there not any more pressure  than i would if i were having friends  over  actually really surprisingly because you  are just so busy  cooking the food you don't have time to  think about the power of the guests  this stunning photo captures german  chancellor angela merkel  grilling him about barbecuing the beef  tenderloin i just learned  through the years just enjoy the moment  and not be intimidated by  anyone because she showed such an  interest and  wanted to know my techniques so she  could maybe duplicate them  among the 54 recipes from the  president's ranch the sweet and smoky  cheeseburger became a staple of what was  dubbed president bush's  cheeseburger diplomacy my food brought  people together countries together  even though you have different views  you're sharing the same food under the  same table  so there's something equalizing about  that nothing else you can talk about the  food  right everybody loves food everyone has  to eat  president bush wasn't the first  president to use uniquely american meals  to forge a bond with world leaders  franklin roosevelt served the king and  queen of england hot dogs at his new  york home in 1939  and president barack obama wasn't afraid  to adopt bush's cheeseburger diplomacy  with russia's dmitry medvedev but he  didn't have wendell so they ate out  the recipes like his mother's hot rolls  or sunday night stacked cheese  enchiladas are straightforward and  approachable  even if you don't really spend much time  in the kitchen which brings us back to  making those burgers  the trick is mixing in the barbecue  sauce before shaping the patties  resulting in a smoky taste and less mess  when you're eating don't be nervous  says the guy who wrote a cookbook laura  bush liked a thin  patty and sharp cheddar cheese thin like  that  so that like that a little thinner throw  the burgers on the grill for a few  minutes at medium heat  add the cheese this smells so good i  need to do more food stories  and it's about time to eat if i can just  get them  off the grill can you tell i spend a lot  of time in the kitchen  well there are other jobs to do with the  burgers finally on the plate  it was time to eat try the pasta salad  too and  eat we did this is fantastic my mother  said always put a little love into  whatever you make so  that's what i try to do oh love him  christmas welcome to our dish yeah and  that's it  don't be thinking like you're going to  take all our great dishes  anything it's good that's cause yeah i  mean it was great yeah no it was  fantastic we love ourselves it is food  diplomacy good stuff learned a lot
 

